From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:47:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Isolate annotation scheduler idle proof from
 ancestor metadata

Problem: native idle test refreshed before its intentional source unlink.
Why: production watches ancestor names and an ancestor IN_ATTRIB is a source
invalidation, even when source contents have not changed. Controlled utime
reproduces the original updated.wait(61) assertion failure in 1.08 seconds;
chmod emits the same native masks and must remain an invalidation.
Root (happened): the scheduler-only idle fixture included shared ancestor
metadata outside its owned input, so another actor could legitimately wake it.
Historical attribution remains unknown: the CI log has no inotify provenance.
Root (not caught): prior quiet-host retries did not inject ancestor metadata.
Recurrence: existing event-loop test never isolated this subscription boundary.

Keep production unchanged. Scope only the long scheduler fixture to its private
source parent, retaining native descriptors, parsing, wait and removal delivery.
Inject owned ancestor utime into the original test. Preserve all original61s,
lease beat, exact read, <1s removal and <500cs/s assertions. Independently test
production ancestor utime/chmod invalidation and unrelated sibling exclusion.

Proof: historical a729187 and base c9d83070 versions of event loop, native watcher
and original test are byte-identical. HERMES_TEST_FILE_RETRIES=0 canonical runs:
baseline file4pass; baseline ID1pass; controlled pre-isolation ID fails at original
idle assertion; fixed native/event suites27pass; fixed isolated ID1pass with
61.01s idle case. Full scripts/check --base origin/main passes.
